{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod","id":673473,"title":"Freddy Krueger in OWoD...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-21T15:32:52-07:00","id":673473,"title":"Freddy Krueger in OWoD...","content":"I think this is long overdue but in honor of Wes Craven who recently passed away, I wonder how his iconic creation, Freddy Krueger would fit into the OWoD at anyway? Of course though we all know Freddy already fought Jason, I wonder how he fairs with the other supernatural denizens in the OWoD like Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, etc and how can they fight him?<br /> <br /> Which in this case as for Vampire, I think the <i>Insomnium</i> discpline (and the Alucinor bloodline) from <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> needs to be imported in Masquerade in order for a Kindred to face Freddy....<br /> <br /> Lastly here's a little gem I found:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKJh5e2aVbs\" data-code=\"YKJh5e2aVbs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YKJh5e2aVbs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:38:05-07:00","id":673533,"title":"","content":"Dream Hunters, a type of hostile memory-spirit that's a frequent threat to Mokole while they delve into Mnesis. Being half-spirit kind of simplifies a lot of plans for Mokole and Bete for fighting against something like Freddy, since they can take steps to make the threat somewhat more &quot;grounded&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T19:13:05-07:00","id":673741,"title":"","content":"I've always figured he wound up being Shadow-eaten with a very advanced and unique understanding of Phantasm (the dream mastery for sure) and Usury (as he feeds on their fears and draws strength and power in the collection of their souls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1738-charon","name":"Charon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T19:20:34-07:00","id":673761,"title":"","content":"He matches almost exactly with being a Spectre with Phantasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T22:17:04-07:00","id":673865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod?p=673761#post673761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He matches almost exactly with being a Spectre with Phantasm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. It was the thing that immediately came to mind. It's just a question of what kind of Spectre is he. Most likely a Doppleganger although I could see arguments for other castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T23:07:35-07:00","id":673878,"title":"","content":"In KOTE there is a Devil Tiger Rite that basically lets you torture someone in their dreams ala Freddy unless they sleep in a holy shrine. Of course this assumes a person taking on the Freddy Role is working as a force of karma rather than random assholishness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:51:21-07:00","id":674598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod?p=673865#post673865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree. It was the thing that immediately came to mind. It's just a question of what kind of Spectre is he. Most likely a Doppleganger although I could see arguments for other castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how he died with anger and sudden violence, he could be a Nephwrack. Or he's a unique case (if you're going with the sixth movie) were he made a deal with dream demons, thus he could've willingly automatically jumped into Spectre status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:17:39-07:00","id":675584,"title":"","content":"I thought the Nephwracks were Doppelgangers that had lost all their Fetters and gotten twisted by Oblivion over time. Isn't it the Mortwights that go directly to spectrehood without passing Go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:23:49-07:00","id":675667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod?p=673878#post673878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In KOTE there is a Devil Tiger Rite that basically lets you torture someone in their dreams ala Freddy unless they sleep in a holy shrine. Of course this assumes a person taking on the Freddy Role is working as a force of karma rather than random assholishness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which book? I couldn't find it in DB: DT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:47:45-07:00","id":675685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod?p=675667#post675667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which book? I couldn't find it in DB: DT.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blood and Silk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:43:52-07:00","id":676928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod?p=675584#post675584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Nephwracks were Doppelgangers that had lost all their Fetters and gotten twisted by Oblivion over time. Isn't it the Mortwights that go directly to spectrehood without passing Go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Opps. My mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:37:58-07:00","id":707593,"title":"","content":"Okay I have a story idea for this to work have Freddy in a Vampire game for example...<br /> <br /> The Prince, Archbishop, or Baron of Cleveland Ohio is interested claiming some territory in Springwood but however there is one problem, it seems that the town's younger population are not only rapidly dying (or alternatively buying from Nightmare 6, all the towns young population are all killed off) but also the adult's population are beginning to act very...strangely, and so they send their agents there to see what's going on...<br /> <br /> I wonder if this could work or someone could come up with a better story/campaign idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 10-18-2015, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T23:13:22-07:00","id":708203,"title":"","content":"Actually it could work, I might not use Vampire. Vampires if we go with Freddie as a wraith could with proper discipline take care of him fairly easily. I might be tempted to write a Nightmare in Springwood story as a straight Wraith chronicle. The pc are agents of the Heiarchy who are investigating the large number of deaths occurring in teens and children of Springwood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T07:43:30-07:00","id":708735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/673473-freddy-krueger-in-owod?p=708203#post708203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it could work, I might not use Vampire. Vampires if we go with Freddie as a wraith could with proper discipline take care of him fairly easily. I might be tempted to write a Nightmare in Springwood story as a straight Wraith chronicle. The pc are agents of the Heiarchy who are investigating the large number of deaths occurring in teens and children of Springwood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well although I always wanted to see how a Vampire vs Freddy fight would have turned out well especially what oneliners Freddy would come up with regarding Vampires and especially pulling some nasty sadistic tricks especially exploiting Vampire weaknesses he would pull on them in their dreams like for example, maybe if a Vampire was in a outdoor area with Freddy, he would probably turn the area instantly into daylight with Freddy laughing in the background while the Vampire burns or anything else since Freddy is pretty omnipotent in the Dreamworld if you take the sequels into account.<br /> <br /> As for Wraith though, I think this might sound like a good idea for a Vampire/Wraith crossover game perhaps? Although major concern though especially the sequels into account, the wraith characters would probably would not last that long INB4 Freddy eats them up to add to his 'chest-o-souls' unless I'm wrong though if Wraiths are different than regular souls.<br /> <br /> So yeah I always thought Freddy would be a formidable adversary though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T08:29:07-07:00","id":708770,"title":"","content":"The fact he eats souls suggests he's possibly a Malfean. That's how they, too, get all big and powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T13:13:34-07:00","id":709196,"title":"","content":"He could certainly be on his way to becoming one if he hasn't quite made it there yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T11:17:04-07:00","id":723715,"title":"","content":"Freddy is likely a Doppleganger on his way to becoming a Nephwrack in service to a Malphean he sends souls to. Objectively, the film series does not follow WoD logic. If you follow the films strictly, the rules can't simulate it since there is not enough time for Freddy to become that powerful. Neither does he deal with the Hierarchy and other opponents he would normally face. If you take the basic concepts and introduce them to the WoD, you need to make changes to recognize how the setting does things. The further you go into the series, the more you are dealing with its own mythos and that mythos's rules don't reflect the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:01:42-07:00","id":742424,"title":"","content":"Oneiromancy from the Sorcerer book might be a good thing to take a look at if you want to really get that down. Can really ruin a person's night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}